64,3,,status,Mio,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
65,3,1,talk,Mio,,"Looking at the options, Ledger Bridge and Clinic Scheduler are software, but we're already swamped with board seats! Fabric Loop and Harvest Sensor need field crews, which will take forever to hire! This is so tough!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,1,talk,George,,"@Mio, we must prioritize the business model over our current schedule. Ledger Bridge and Clinic Scheduler align with our successful exits. Between them, Clinic Scheduler's focus on independent practices suggests the high retention I found.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,1,talk,May,,"@George, I'm worried about the cash. Clinic Scheduler and Ledger Bridge are software, meaning our credit line is useless for them. If they need a sudden cash injection, we're relying solely on those dwindling reserves.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,1,talk,Rin,,Wait! Fabric Loop and Harvest Sensor have things moving around or in the field! That means we can actually check the numbers ourselves instead of just trusting a dashboard! I like that way better!,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,1,talk,Mizuki,,"@Rin, that is a dangerous trade-off. Fabric Loop and Harvest Sensor involve physical hardware and logistics, which my research shows lead to severe deployment delays and supply chain bottlenecks. We cannot risk another stalled launch.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,2,talk,Mio,,"@Mizuki, you're right about the delays! But @George, if we pick Clinic Scheduler, who is going to manage it? We're already at our limit with software boards! We'll be working weekends just to keep up!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Mizuki"",""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,2,talk,George,,"@Mio, we can find a way to manage our time, but we cannot manufacture a successful exit from a flawed model. Clinic Scheduler offers the stability and retention we need to ensure this investment actually pays off.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,2,talk,May,,"@George, stability is a dream if we go bankrupt first. If we pick Clinic Scheduler, we're betting everything on reserves that are already leaking. We need a candidate that doesn't put our liquidity at extreme risk.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,2,talk,Rin,,"@May, but if we pick a software one, we're just guessing on the numbers! I'd rather have a little more work at the end of the quarter than a big mystery that might be a lie!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@Rin, the ""mystery"" of a dashboard is manageable; the mystery of why a product hasn't launched after nine months is not. Clinic Scheduler deals with medical records, which means a long security review. Ledger Bridge is the safest bet for speed.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,3,talk,Mio,,"@Mizuki, if Ledger Bridge is the fastest, maybe that's the way! But @George, we still have the board seat problem. Can we really handle another software company without burning out? I'm really worried about our bandwidth!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Mizuki"",""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,3,talk,George,,"@Mio, burnout is a management issue, not a financial one. We must prioritize the asset's viability. Ledger Bridge is lean and fits our success profile, but Clinic Scheduler's target market is far more resilient to price changes.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,3,talk,May,,"@George, resilience doesn't matter if we can't fund the growth. Ledger Bridge is leaner, which means fewer follow-on calls. If we're this low on cash, we can't afford a ""resilient"" company that's expensive to maintain.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,3,talk,Rin,,"But Ledger Bridge is just another dashboard! I'm tired of not knowing the truth! If we pick Harvest Sensor, we can see the sensors in the dirt! That's way more exciting and honest!","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,3,talk,Mizuki,,"@Rin, excitement is not a strategy. Harvest Sensor is a recipe for supply chain delays and audit nightmares. If we want a predictable path to revenue without draining our reserves or stalling for months, Ledger Bridge is the only logical choice.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
80,3,4,talk,Mio,,"I'm still worried about our time, but @Mizuki and @May make a strong case. If Ledger Bridge is the leanest and fastest, it's the only way we survive without collapsing! I vote for Ledger Bridge!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Mizuki"",""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
81,3,4,talk,George,,"I must disagree with the shift toward Ledger Bridge. While lean, Clinic Scheduler's target market is far more stable. We cannot sacrifice long-term retention for short-term convenience. I vote for Clinic Scheduler.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
82,3,4,talk,May,,I can't risk a high-maintenance investment when our reserves are leaking and our credit line is so restrictive. Ledger Bridge is the leanest option and the safest for our cash flow. I vote for Ledger Bridge.,"{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
83,3,4,talk,Rin,,"I don't like the dashboards, but I don't want us to go bankrupt or be too tired to play! If everyone else says it's the safest, I'll go with it. I vote for Ledger Bridge!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
84,3,4,talk,Mizuki,,"I agree with the majority. While Clinic Scheduler has potential, the security review for medical data is a bottleneck we cannot afford. Ledger Bridge offers the most predictable deployment timeline and the lowest financial risk. I vote for Ledger Bridge.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
